            "text": "E-commerce fraud detection using a two-layer graph convolutional network (GCN) integrated with large language models (LLMs) demonstrates high precision for legitimate transactions but struggles with low recall for fraudulent cases. The model achieves near-perfect precision (0.98) and recall (1.00) for non-fraud (Class 0), minimizing false positives, yet detects only 5% of fraudulent transactions (Class 1), with 31,726 false positives.",
